  "question": {
    "text": "If the line $\\frac{2-x}{3}=\\frac{3 y-2}{4 \\lambda+1}=4-z$ makes a right angle with the line $\\frac{x+3}{3 \\mu}=\\frac{1-2 y}{6}=\\frac{5-z}{7}$, then $4 \\lambda+9 \\mu$ is equal to :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "4",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "13",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "5",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "6",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\frac{2-x}{3}=\\frac{3 y-2}{4 \\lambda+1}=4-z...(1)$\n$\\frac{x-2}{(-3)}=\\frac{y-\\frac{2}{3}}{\\left(\\frac{4 \\lambda+1}{3}\\right)}=\\frac{z-4}{(-1)}$\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{x+3}{3 \\mu}=\\frac{1-2 y}{6}=\\frac{5-z}{7}...(2) \\\\ & \\frac{x+3}{3 \\mu}=\\frac{y-\\frac{1}{2}}{(-3)}=\\frac{z-5}{(-7)} \\\\ & \\text { Right angle } \\Rightarrow(-3)(3 \\mu)+\\left(\\frac{4 \\lambda+1}{3}\\right)(-3)+(-1)(-7)=0 \\\\ & -9 \\mu-4 \\lambda-1+7=0 \\\\ & 4 \\lambda+9 \\mu=6\\end{aligned}$"
  }
